@startuml
title SplitSmart - platform and trust boundaries (proposed)
left to right direction
actor "Account holder / group member" as User
actor "Group reviewer / manager" as Reviewer
rectangle "Desktop MVP (local; proposed)" {
  component "Java Swing client" as Swing
  component "Application + domain core" as Core
  database "Local SQLite DB" as LocalDB
  folder "Private local receipt files" as LocalReceipts
  Swing --> Core : local use cases
  Core --> LocalDB : repositories
  Core --> LocalReceipts : receipt port
}
rectangle "Full product (future proposal; not in repository)" {
  component "Web client" as Web
  component "Android client" as Android
  component "iOS client" as IOS
  component "Authenticated API\n(authoritative use cases)" as API
  database "Shared relational DB" as SharedDB
  cloud "Private receipt object store" as ObjectStore
  Web --> API : TLS / authenticated requests
  Android --> API : TLS / authenticated requests
  IOS --> API : TLS / authenticated requests
  API --> SharedDB : transactional persistence
  API --> ObjectStore : authorized receipt access
}
User --> Swing : desktop only
Reviewer --> Swing : desktop workflow
User --> Web : future
User --> Android : future
User --> IOS : future
note bottom of Swing
  Local account/data state is not
  shared across devices. Does not
  satisfy FR-010.
end note
note bottom of API
  Future architecture only.
  No API/mobile/web implementation
  was observed.
end note
@enduml
